[decoded] "Based on the repeated notes provided, here is a summary of how the hybrid model processes a token:\n\n*   **GatedDeltaNet Processing:** For every token, the model updates a recurrent state per value head by first predicting the value from the current state, calculating the difference (residual) between the actual value and that prediction, and writing this scaled difference back as a rank-one update to the state.\n*   **Hybrid Architecture:** The architecture alternates between three GatedDeltaNet layers (which handle local, sequential updates) and one full attention layer (which handles global context).\n*   **Context Growth:** The **full attention layer** is the component that grows with the length of the context, as it maintains a classic cache of keys and values and attends over every earlier position using partial rotary embeddings."
